  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "The question needs nitrate and phosphate in micromoles per kilogram at 1025 kg/m3, while CMIP6 BGC concentrations are stored per unit volume, so the conversion must be applied before N:P ratios, regressions and volume metrics.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Convert `no3`/`po4` from mol m-3 to µmol kg-1 before comparing with WOA23 µmol kg-1: µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ; the question prescribes \"a constant density of 1025 kg/m3\" where the fragment asks for in-situ density below the surface, so the question's version is followed and the difference stated (about 1 % in deep and fresh water), quoting `attrs['density_assumption']`.",
        "N:P is a ratio of two tracers converted with the same ρ, so it is scale-invariant: the 12 and 14–18 thresholds, the headline mean N:P and the ratio of means need no density; absolute NO3/PO4 in µmol kg-1 and the regression do."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "Comparing the three models with WOA23 requires valid-cell masks to be handled consistently so that ratios and regression statistics are not computed over artificial or mismatched land-sea masks.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build one shared mask with `build_comparison_mask` and apply `.where(mask)` to all four sources before any cell-by-cell statistic or scatter/regression sample; with WOA23 as the reference the default `ocean_only=True` is right. Report the cell counts next to the metrics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The basin means explicitly use the WOA23 basin mask with marginal seas folded into parent oceans and Southern/Arctic excluded, so the chosen partition constrains the Pacific, Atlantic and Indian results.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Basin values use the WOA23 mask via `select_basin`/`load_basin_mask` with `include_marginal_seas=True` (the Ofx `basin` field is not archived); state which mask was used, whether the Southern Ocean is separate, and that `depth_dependent=False` surface labels are what a named ocean usually means."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The percentage-of-water-volume results and any global/basin water-volume measures must be volume-weighted using volcello rather than counting cells equally.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Layer means and exceedance percentages must be volume-weighted with NaN-aware weights on the same cells: `compute_basic_stat(op='volume_weighted_mean')`, and `compute_exceedance_fraction` (which returns the m3 behind the percentage — report it).",
        "Label the N:P: `compute_ratio` gives the cell-by-cell ratio (headline), the ratio of means is the two volume-weighted means divided; the question's OLS with \"each cell weighted equally\" is a plain unweighted fit, unlike the area weighting `compute_difference_metrics` applies by default."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "N:P is a nonlinear ratio, so computing it from monthly-mean nitrate and phosphate is not identical to averaging monthly ratios, which affects how the headline mean N:P and time-averaging caveat are stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "N:P is a nonlinear diagnostic, so state the order used: ratio computed per month then averaged, or ratio of the 1971-2000 mean fields.",
        "Average the monthly fields over the period with `temporal_aggregate` (day weights); `compute_basic_stat(op='mean', dim='time')` weights months equally and is not a time average."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bgc-model-structure-comparison",
      "severity": "info",
      "path": "datasets/bgc-model-structure-comparison.md",
      "sha256": "4ef3e4ab0b9741f6ab5d15f88cfbdf8b7366c82b093ce99e26f1707a2a788e54",
      "reason": "The models differ in stoichiometry and nutrient cycling, which is needed to interpret cross-model N:P differences and whether they reproduce denitrification-related low-N:P water.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Interpret the spread through model structure: CESM2 has variable C:P, GFDL-ESM4 fixed N:P per plankton type, MPI-ESM1-2-LR prescribed Redfield; \"not detailed in paper\" does not mean a feature is absent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
